# How to cite PRISMT. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo reads
# .zenodo.json for the archived record (keep the two in step: tests/python/test_docs.py checks it).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PRISMT, please cite the software (this record) and the PRISMt paper listed
  under references.
type: software
title: "PRISMT: transformers for trial-structured neural and behavioral recordings, driven from MATLAB"
abstract: >-
  PRISMT lets experimentalists train the PRISMt transformer on trial-structured recordings
  (brain activity, behavior, or both) from a MATLAB app, without writing code. It classifies
  trial conditions and learns the structure of the recordings with a masked autoencoder,
  tests on held-out animals by cross-validation, and compares every result with simple
  reference models.
